= Hypertext Transfer Protocol — Technical =

HTTP semantics are version-independent at the conceptual level: methods express request intent, status codes characterize responses, and fields carry metadata. HTTP/1.1, HTTP/2, and HTTP/3 use different message framing and transport details while preserving shared semantics.

== Modeling / implementation cautions ==
* HTTP ≠ HTML
* HTTP ≠ World Wide Web
* HTTP method ≠ application business operation necessarily

